atlas institutional

architecture credential-boundary
  canonical_name CredentialBoundary
  family institutional
  domain Institutional / Credentials
  layer institutional
  semantic_question What does each provider require before this estate can read from it, which of those values are set, generated or missing, how is a credential applied to a request and verified, and how is that kept private?
  purpose The dedicated credential boundary ExternalAuthIntent points at. Providers are declared in CUE (fields, where a person gets them, what the estate can generate, how a credential is applied as headers or query, how it is verified, what the estate tells the provider) or derived from a JSON OpenAPI document's security schemes. Values are sealed with AES-256-GCM under a private key file with the provider and field as associated data. A loopback-only page lets a signed-in Bonfyre admin set, generate, clear and check credentials; admin-only MCP tools on the OAuth gateway do the same; the reheat asks the boundary for a credentialed source's request and waits while a required field is missing.
  maturity implemented
  consumes BonfyreAuth
  consumes ExternalAuthIntent
  publishes CredentialProviderStatus
  publishes CredentialedRequest
  node_types CredentialProvider
  node_types SealedCredentialField
  node_types CredentialVerification
  invariant a value is sealed with AES-256-GCM under a 32-byte key file that must not be readable by group or others; the provider and field are the associated data, so a sealed value moved to another slot does not open
  invariant a stored value is never shown again; status answers set, generated or missing with the last four characters of a sensitive value only; a generated value may be revealed once, at generation
  invariant no value reaches argv, a receipt, the weather, a log, the audit or a status answer; verification and credentialed reads hand the address and headers to curl on its standard input
  invariant the page listens on 127.0.0.1 only, answers only to a loopback Host (421 otherwise), admits only a session BonfyreAuth authorizes as a Bonfyre admin, and accepts a write only with the session's HMAC CSRF token and a loopback Origin; it is never cached or framed
  invariant a credentialed census read waits (no fetch, no receipt) while a required field is missing, and its receipt records the plain address without the credential
  invariant an OpenAPI document's apiKey (header or query), bearer and basic schemes become fields with how they apply; an OAuth client-credentials scheme is exchanged by the boundary itself and its token cached sealed, so a declared OAuth service is readable once its client credentials are set
  invariant a provider that documents a public default (an unauthenticated key a provider publishes for trials) is used until a real credential is set, and its status says so rather than claiming a credential exists
  invariant what the estate can make, it makes: bootstrap generates every declared generator-backed field that is missing, without showing a value, and is idempotent
  invariant the moment a provider becomes ready the boundary runs the declared on-ready hook with that provider's id and nothing else, so reads that were waiting for a credential resume without a person
  invariant every set, generate, clear, verify, apply and sign-in is audited without its value
  invariant a value belongs to one account at its provider: the store keys it by provider, account and field, and a named account joins the associated data, so two people's keys for one provider never share a slot and a value copied into another account's slot does not open; the empty account is the estate's own and keeps the original binding, so stores sealed before accounts existed migrate in place and still open
  invariant only the estate account tells the on-ready hook and only it is served by the loopback page; a named account is reached by --account on the command line
  forbidden_inference a stored credential -> authority, provider admission, spend approval or an effect right
  forbidden_inference a verified credential -> the provider's data being true, lawful to republish or worth reading
  forbidden_inference an MCP-set value -> a private value; it travelled through that agent session
  forbidden_inference a declared provider -> a credential having been obtained
  forbidden_inference an account label on a sealed value -> the provider's own account identity, or proof of who signed up; it names where the value is kept apart, not who authenticated
  known_gap YAML OpenAPI documents are not read; they must be converted to JSON first
  known_gap only the reheat consumes credentials; provider model calls, MusicBrainz, AcoustID lookups and OpenCorporates reads still have no credentialed caller
  known_gap Aurekai publishes no OpenAPI document of its own yet; the generated API client credential has no endpoint that checks it
  known_gap no credential is set on the estate by this change; Podcast Index recent episodes waits until one is
  known_gap the installed estate binary predates accounts; the store migrates the first time this build opens it, and no consumer binding names an account yet
  known_gap the page is reached by an SSH tunnel to loopback; no Cloudflare route exists to it and none should be added, but that route list is remote configuration this estate cannot see
  source_path schemas/control/provider-credentials.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCredentials/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCredentials/Makefile
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCredentials/tests/credentials_test.sh
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/src/main.c
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tests/credentialed_reheat_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCredentials/tools/discover_credential_needs.mjs
  source_path scripts/bonfyre-credential-ready
  source_path integrations/mcp/bonfyre_oauth_gateway.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/patch_credentials_tools.py.archive
  witness integrations/mcp/bonfyre_oauth_gateway.mjs carries the credential tool definitions and handlers directly; the former Python text-insertion step is retired because it had no caller and the behavior is now authored in the gateway
  source_path integrations/mcp/bonfyre_oauth_gateway.mjs
  witness cmd/BonfyreCredentials/tests/credentials_test.sh proves a private key is created once and a readable one refused, a sealed value is absent from the store as plaintext and shown only by its last four, a Podcast Index request carries sha1(key+secret+epoch), a missing required field refuses, a sealed value moved to another field does not open, a generated secret is shown once, an OpenAPI document's five schemes become seven fields with header, query and OAuth notes, the page refuses a non-loopback Host, refuses a non-admin, sets a strict http-only cookie, refuses a write without CSRF or from another origin, seals an admin write without echoing it, verifies against a stub provider with the stored bearer token, never shows a stored or generated value again, and audits every act without a value; no credential appeared in any process's arguments
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/credentialed_reheat_test.sh proves a credentialed census row waits with no fetch or receipt while its key is missing, then reads with the provider's header and query credential once set, retaining the authenticated body while the receipt and weather hold neither the key nor the signed address
  witness 2026-09-17 on the estate the organ's test and the credentialed reheat test passed under GCC 13 and system OpenSSL; production created /etc/bonfyre/credentials.key (0600, service user), started bonfyre-credentials.service listening on 127.0.0.1:18910 only, which answered 200 on loopback, 421 to Host aurekai.work and was unreachable on the public address; status listed 15 providers with none ready; the OAuth MCP gateway gained the six admin credential tools by anchored patch and restarted active
  witness cmd/BonfyreCredentials/tests/credentials_test.sh also proves a documented public default is used and named as one until a key is set, that a provider still missing a field does not announce itself ready, that the moment it is ready the hook is told its id and nothing else, that a client-credentials token is exchanged, applied and cached sealed rather than exchanged again, and that verify-all checks every ready provider including one on its public default
  witness cmd/BonfyreCredentials/tests/accounts_test.sh proves a store sealed by the binary before accounts migrates in place with its value still applying, two named accounts and the estate account hold three values for one provider and field that each apply only under their own account, status and clear touch only the named account and the audit names it, a sealed value copied across accounts does not open, an account name outside the allowed letters is refused, and a missing or malformed providers file is named instead of printing an unset parser buffer
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCredentials/tests/accounts_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreCredentials/tests/discover_credential_needs_test.mjs proves descriptor priority excludes derived WordPress JSON API and refused channels, exact WorkGraph host discovery retains an OpenAPI description and imports only credential schemes, payment presentation remains economic evidence, and failed observation cannot replay a preceding receipt or body
  source_lineage 2026-09-17 private credentials page for everything that needs auth

interaction credential-boundary-signs-credentialed-reads
  source credential-boundary
  destination foreign-twin
  relation issues_credentialed_request
  preserves the provider's declared header and query placement and the plain source address for the receipt
  drops every credential value from receipts, weather and arguments
  forbidden_inference a credentialed observation -> remote authority or a right to republish
  invalidates_on sealed_field changes, provider declarations, key rotation
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/credentialed_reheat_test.sh
